# mix_tracks.buda at DOUBLE the signal density — 16 tracks per period, not 8.
#
# Produced mechanically by `tools/double_track_density.py`: each `SIGNAL w s`
# slot becomes two `SIGNAL w/2 s/2` slots, so the pair occupies exactly the
# footprint the single slot had.  Period, signal metal and the declared
# `def_layer` overheads are therefore all UNCHANGED from mix_tracks.buda — this
# is the same wiring budget divided more finely, at half the bit pitch.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   cp flow/rnr/mix_tracks.buda flow/rnr/mix_tracks_2x.buda
#   tools/double_track_density.py flow/rnr/mix_tracks_2x.buda
#
# Used ONLY by the `*_2x` flow clones.  The originals stay on mix_tracks.buda:
# their congestion is what the healer and doomed-seat vehicles exist to
# exercise, and removing it would delete that coverage.  See
# docs/internal/track_density_doubling.md.
# From tracks_for_channel_stress.buda, but with four top:

def_layer 2 M2 H LOW 55.56
def_layer 3 M3 V LOW 55.56
def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 55.56
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 55.56
def_layer 6 M6 H TOP 66.67
def_layer 7 M7 V TOP 58.97

# Track patterns are REQUIRED for Detailed NUTS
# Format: <layer_id> <origin> [<type> <width> <spacing>] ...
def_track_pattern 2 -100  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.25)x8  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.25)x8
def_track_pattern 3    0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.25)x8  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.25)x8
def_track_pattern 4 -200  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.25)x8  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.25)x8
def_track_pattern 5    0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.25)x8  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.25)x8
def_track_pattern 6 -400  POWER 3 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.5)x8  GROUND 3 1  (SIGNAL 0.5 0.5)x8
def_track_pattern 7 -600  POWER 6 2  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x8  GROUND 6 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x8

report_overhead
